WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.332
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.520
SPEAKER: ReCAPTCHA has over a
decade of experience defending

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.860
the internet, and
reCaPTCHA Enterprise

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.070
builds on that experience to
provide frictionless security

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:16.360
for your business.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:19.960
ReCAPTCHA Enterprise is built
on the existing reCAPTCHA API

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.690
and offers granular
insight and detection,

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.790
allowing you to
understand and tune

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.710
the protection you
need for your website.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:30.880
Let's take a look at what makes
reCAPTCHA Enterprise different.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.220
There are three primary
advantages to note here.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:37.810
First, reCAPTCHA Enterprise
provides a frictionless user

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:41.470
experience, leveraging advanced
risk analysis techniques that

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:43.690
distinguish between
humans and bots

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.720
without requiring customers
to complete a challenge.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:50.140
Second, reCAPTCHA Enterprise
offers enhanced detection

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:53.830
with granular scores, reason
codes for risky events,

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:57.580
mobile app SDKs, password
breach and leak detection,

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.370
multifactor authentication,
and the ability

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:03.470
to tune your own
site-specific model.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:05.590
And finally,
reCAPTCHA Enterprise

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:10.570
provides the support, like the
SLAs and SLOs, that you expect

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.940
from a Google Cloud product.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:16.320
So if you expect a lot from your
reCAPTCHA integration in usage

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.130
or in support, or if you want
to detect automated attacks

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.900
or threats against
your website that

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.740
may originate from human
actors, mobile emulators, or bot

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:29.340
software, then reCAPTCHA
Enterprise is right for you.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.400
For existing reCAPTCHA
v2 and v3 users,

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.460
we've made it a priority
to make migration simple--

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:38.880
so simple, in fact, that it
should only take two minutes.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.720
First, navigate to your project
in the Google Cloud console.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:47.460
You'll need to enable the
reCAPTCHA Enterprise API.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.560
While you're here, be sure
to note your project ID.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:56.030
Second, navigate to
google.com/reCAPTCHA/admin

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:58.520
to find your existing
reCAPTCHA site key.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.460
You can find your existing
v2 and v3 site keys

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.020
under Settings.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:05.690
Click the cog icon to
open the Settings view,

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:09.380
and then expand the section
labeled reCAPTCHA keys.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.960
Copy the site key.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.120
To perform the migration,
you can use Cloud Shell.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:19.350
Note that your account will need
to be either a project owner

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:22.860
or have the reCAPTCHA
Enterprise admin IAM role.

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.240
A major benefit of
using Cloud Shell

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.030
is that all authentication
is handled automatically,

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:33.160
as the Cloud Shell
instance is already

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:36.880
tied to your user account
and its existing credentials.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.860
However, if this
is the first time

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:41.080
you run a command that
requires credentials,

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:45.630
you will need to authorize
Cloud Shell first.

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:47.700
To perform the key
migration, you only

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.380
need a single command--

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:53.910
run gcloud alpha
recaptcha keys migrate.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:57.390
And specify the v2 or
v3 reCAPTCHA site key

00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:01.020
you wish to migrate and
the project ID of the cloud

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:03.600
project where you enabled
the reCAPTCHA Enterprise

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.860
API earlier.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:06.840
You should see a
confirmation that your key

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:09.650
has been successfully migrated.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.010
Back in the Cloud console,
we can see our migrated key

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:14.330
under Security--

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:16.200
reCAPTCHA Enterprise.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.530
Here, we can see analytics and
manage the key moving forward.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:23.720
And that is how you can easily
migrate your existing reCAPTCHA

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:28.000
v2 and v3 site keys to
reCAPTCHA Enterprise for truly

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.770
frictionless security.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.170
To learn more about
reCAPTCHA Enterprise,

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:35.030
go to cloud.google.com/recaptcha
enterprise.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:41.130
[MUSIC PLAYING]

